<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p><m>A</m> is <m>({-2}, {-2})</m> and <m>B</m> is <m>({4}, {-2})</m>.</p><p>Condition 1: <m>PA</m> <m>\le</m> <m>{5}</m>.</p><p>Condition 2: <m>P</m> is nearer to <m>A</m> than to <m>B</m>.</p><p>For each point <m>P</m>, decide which conditions it satisfies.</p><ol><li><div><m>({1}, {-3})</m> [ both conditions | condition 1 only | condition 2 only | neither condition ]  </div></li><li><div><m>({-6}, {-1})</m> [ both conditions | condition 1 only | condition 2 only | neither condition ]  </div></li><li><div><m>({2}, {-5})</m> [ both conditions | condition 1 only | condition 2 only | neither condition ]  </div></li><li><div><m>({-5}, {3})</m> [ both conditions | condition 1 only | condition 2 only | neither condition ]  </div></li></ol></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>Condition 1 compares <m>PA^2</m> with <m>{5}^2 = {25}</m>. A point exactly <m>{5}</m> from <m>A</m> is on the circle: it does satisfy <m>PA \le {5}</m>. Condition 2 compares <m>PA^2</m> with <m>PB^2</m>. A point on the perpendicular bisector of <m>AB</m> is the same distance from both, so it is nearer to neither.</p><ol><li><p><m>({1}, {-3})</m>: <m>PA^2 = {10}</m>, <m>PB^2 = {10}</m>. Condition 1 holds; condition 2 fails.</p></li><li><p><m>({-6}, {-1})</m>: <m>PA^2 = {17}</m>, <m>PB^2 = {101}</m>. Condition 1 holds; condition 2 holds.</p></li><li><p><m>({2}, {-5})</m>: <m>PA^2 = {25}</m>, <m>PB^2 = {13}</m>. Condition 1 holds; condition 2 fails.</p></li><li><p><m>({-5}, {3})</m>: <m>PA^2 = {34}</m>, <m>PB^2 = {106}</m>. Condition 1 fails; condition 2 holds.</p></li></ol></p></solution>
    <answer><p>condition 1 only</p></answer>
    <answer><p>both conditions</p></answer>
    <answer><p>condition 1 only</p></answer>
    <answer><p>condition 2 only</p></answer>
</stack-static>